  "narrative": "The new battery gives a coherent, largely additive picture for the three strongest binary predictors, while giving little support for the smaller interactions. H56 is decisive for feature_037: among participants without feature_010 and without feature_002, the signed stronger-dependency contrast is +0.814 [0.768,0.860], far above the +0.15 threshold. Together with H43 and H45, which show feature_037=1 associated with much stronger dependency within feature_010=1 and feature_002=1, and with H44/H46 showing the same effect in the corresponding complements, this supports a strong dataset-specific feature_037 association that is not merely an artifact of overlap with the other two predictors. Persistence after conditioning, however, still does not imply causal independence or biological independence.\n\nH49 shows the analogous overlap-conditional weaker-dependency association for feature_002 within feature_037=1: +0.790 [0.661,0.920]. Combined with H42, H50, and the reciprocal feature_037-in-feature_002 evidence, this completes the core direct-effect pattern. I accept H43, H45, H49, and H56 as scientifically meaningful dataset-specific associations. These claims remain observational and may reflect correlated latent dependency structure rather than mutually independent causal pathways.\n\nThe interaction battery does not support meaningful modification among these predictors. H54 estimates feature_037 modification by feature_010=1 as +0.070 [-0.053,0.192], which is small, imprecise, and centered well below threshold. H57 and H58 are even less supportive: H57 is negative relative to the claimed attenuation direction, and H58 is also negative relative to the claimed attenuation direction and compatible with null. I reject and close these interaction claims as unsupported in this dataset. They are not definitive proofs of absence because some intervals include threshold-magnitude positive values, but the available evidence does not justify allocating further validation or follow-up to these particular interaction contrasts.\n\nThe log_PFS interactions are similarly uninformative. H60 for feature_037 is +0.040 [-0.085,0.164], H61 for feature_010 is near null and opposite to the claimed attenuation direction, and H62 for feature_002 is -0.128 [-0.259,0.002], which is in the opposite signed direction from attenuation and mostly excludes a claimed-direction threshold effect. Thus, none of the registered longer-log_PFS attenuation hypotheses is supported. This is an observed contrast result only; it does not establish that log_PFS has no clinically relevant modification with larger samples or different endpoint definitions.\n\nThe clean feature_063 stratum is now much clearer: H55 gives feature_063=1 associated with stronger dependency when feature_037, feature_010, and feature_002 are all absent, +0.252 [0.169,0.335]. This is above threshold and has adequate cells, so I accept it as a dataset-specific association. H51 validation had crossed the threshold at a stringent correction despite similar magnitude, so independent validation of H55 is the most useful next use of validation resources. If validation excludes the threshold, feature_063 becomes a much more robust conditional signal; if it does not, H52/H55 should still be treated as discovery-supported subgroup candidates rather than broadly confirmed claims.\n\nH59 for feature_003 in the same triple-strong-absent stratum is +0.144 [0.083,0.204]. This is consistently positive with earlier near-threshold feature_003 results, but its point estimate does not exceed the 0.15 threshold and the interval crosses threshold. I leave it unresolved and deferred rather than accepting it as meaningful. It represents a possible subthreshold association, not evidence of a threshold-exceeding effect.\n\nI request validation for H55 because it is the smallest currently accepted new signal and the validation evidence needed most strongly for the feature_063 family. I also register direct overlap-conditional tests of feature_010 within feature_002=1 and feature_002 within feature_010=1 to complete the two-way overlap structure for the two weaker-dependency predictors. H47 and the untested marginal screens H30-H36 are reactivated because broad exploration still matters after the dominant predictor structure has been characterized.",
  "research_notes": "Current dataset-specific accepted core: feature_037=1 strongly associated with stronger dependency overall, validated, and in feature_010=0, feature_002=0, feature_010=1, feature_002=1, and the clean feature_010=0/feature_002=0 stratum. feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 strongly associated with weaker dependency overall and in feature_037=0 complements; feature_002=1 also persists within feature_037=1. feature_063=1 is associated with stronger dependency within feature_010=0 and in the triple-strong-absent stratum; H55 validation requested because feature_063 is the key smaller candidate and previous H51 validation crossed threshold. feature_003 remains a consistent but subthreshold positive candidate.\n\nInteraction evidence is negative or inconclusive for attenuation: feature_037 x feature_010, feature_037 x feature_002, feature_010 x feature_002, and all three upper-half log_PFS interactions are rejected/closed. Do not interpret these as proof of no modification; they are unsupported in this dataset.\n\nNext priorities: (1) assess H55 validation when delivered; (2) run H47 to complete direct feature_010 effect within feature_037=1; (3) run newly registered direct overlap tests feature_010 within feature_002=1 and feature_002 within feature_010=1 if cells remain adequate; (4) run untested broad marginal screens H30-H36. Continue to avoid interpreting conditional persistence as causal independence or biological mechanism.",
